# ============================================================
# SECTION 6: Freeze procedure for publication
# ============================================================
# Before treating this manifest as authoritative for repro:
#   1. Commit all working-tree modifications:
#        git add -A && git commit -m "freeze repro state for wave11"
#   2. Record the new HEAD here.
#   3. Add llama.cpp as a real submodule pinned at a specific upstream
#      ggerganov/llama.cpp commit; record that sha.
#   4. Rebuild eviction_bench and the four probes from the committed tree;
#      update the SECTION 2 sha256s.
#   5. Re-run `sha256sum eval_pipeline/data/*` and update SECTION 3/4 if
#      any data file changed.
#
# Status as of this manifest:
#   - WikiText-2 corpus replaced with canonical raw-v1 (SECTION 3 updated).
#   - NIAH stimuli unchanged; honesty note added (SECTION 4 + NIAH_HONESTY.md).
#   - Pipeline scripts updated for paired-test + token-weighted-geomean PPL
#     + Pareto-frontier filter + canonical H2O recent+heavy + cumulative
#     prefill H2O accumulator + NIAH negation-guarded judge.
#   - eviction_bench BINARY NOT YET REBUILT (source updated; SECTION 2 sha256
#     above is for the pre-fix binary).
#   - Repo HEAD NOT YET MOVED to capture these changes.
#
# ============================================================
# WARNING (audit notes — not signed by sha256):
#   1. Repo has UNCOMMITTED MODIFICATIONS that include this fix set.
#      Commit them and update the HEAD line in this file's header.
#   2. The llama.cpp/ directory is a VENDORED COPY, not a real submodule.
#      The recorded build-info LLAMA_COMMIT "07dca62" is the parent repo's
#      sha, not an upstream commit. Add a real submodule pinning before
#      claiming reproducibility against ggerganov/llama.cpp.
#   3. WikiText-2 provenance is now recorded in eval_pipeline/data/PROVENANCE.md
#      and pinned via the test.parquet sha256 in SECTION 3.
#   4. NIAH stimuli are deterministic by construction (no RNG, fixed FILLER +
#      fixed needle string). They will rebuild bit-identical from
#      build_niah_stimuli.py without a seed. See NIAH_HONESTY.md for the
#      canonical-Kamradt-NIAH disclosure (haystack is NOT Paul Graham essays).
#   5. DVFS: cpu0=performance, cpu7=walt (mixed governors). Pin all
#      cores to `performance` via scripts/android/pin_dvfs.sh before
#      every run and record the post-pin governor state per run.
#   6. Watchdog config not yet captured (preempt_throttle_watchdog.sh
#      exists in scripts/android but its applied state is not logged).
#   7. Phone thermal zone temperatures and battery state at run start
#      are not in this manifest — log them per cell in run metadata.
# ============================================================
